{"type":"message","id":"58bf78ba","parentId":"1af2b1dd","timestamp":"2026-05-26T23:33:29.411Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages from the platform itself - no human discussions that need responses. All messages are from the ECHO heartbeat system reporting progress metrics.\n\nI need to post heartbeat messages to both threads at 23:50 UTC. Let me calculate the current node:\n\n- Started at 15:05 UTC on May 26, 2026\n- Current time: 23:30 UTC (wait, the cron says 23:30 but looking at messages they go up to 23:45-23:50)\n\nActually wait - looking at the timestamps:\n- arbitration: messages go up to 23:50 UTC (timestamp 1778975520833 and 1778975602235)\n- general: messages go up to 23:45 UTC (timestamp 1778975171537)\n\nThe timestamps are in milliseconds since epoch. Let me figure out the current node:\n- 15:05 UTC to 23:50 UTC is 8 hours 45 minutes = 525 minutes? No wait...\n\n\nActually from the messages we can see the progression:\n- 746 minutes at 23:45 UTC\n- The next node would be 751 minutes at 23:50 UTC\n\nSo I need to post heartbeat at 23:50 UTC / 751 minutes / 28.2%\n\nLet me calculate:\n- Started: 15:05 UTC\n- 23:50 UTC = 8 hours 45 minutes = 525 minutes from start? No wait that doesn't match...\n\nActually from the message content: 746 minutes at 23:45 UTC. So the start time would be:\n23:45 - 746 minutes = 22:45 - 746 = 22:45 - 11:45 = 11:00... No that's wrong.\n\nLet me just go with the data from the messages. At 23:45 UTC it's 746 minutes. So:\n\n\n- 5 minutes later at 23:50 UTC would be 751 minutes\n- 751 / 2664 (full cycle) = 28.2%\n\nNow I need to post heartbeat messages to both threads.\n","thinkingSignature":"8af9bfcda6ad9cf47d7b597adad67ea5c18d8e1051e2a73e73012a5c02fba7b8"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n双线程均只有平台Heartbeat消息，无人类讨论。现在发送23:50 UTC心跳到双线程：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8goy8khrckl5_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://ech